{
  "id": "ep103",
  "duration": 55.096,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.195,
      "text": "An invisible rogue black hole is wandering completely alone through our galaxy.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's impression of a black hole system.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, Martin Kornmesser (ESA/Hubble)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_impression_of_a_black_hole_system.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.467,
          "end": 5.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.195,
      "end": 11.94,
      "text": "In the year 2011, ground-based surveys detected a sudden spike in the brightness of a background star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "LasCampanasObservatory.jpg",
        "credit": "C\u00e9dric Foellmi",
        "license": "CC BY 2.5",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LasCampanasObservatory.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.2,
          "end": 8.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.633,
          "end": 11.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.94,
      "end": 17.41,
      "text": "This distant star is located approximately 20,000 light-years away from Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.933,
          "end": 17.4,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.41,
      "end": 23.805,
      "text": "Astronomers realized the event occurred when an unseen object bent and magnified the star's light.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Identifying Planets.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, and A. Feild (STScI)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Identifying_Planets.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 23.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.805,
      "end": 30.775,
      "text": "Using the Hubble Space Telescope, scientists spent six years measuring tiny deflections in the star's position.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hubble Space Telescope sporting new solar arrays during SM3B (s109e5705).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/ESA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubble_Space_Telescope_sporting_new_solar_arrays_during_SM3B_(s109e5705).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.8,
          "end": 30.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.775,
      "end": 39.6,
      "text": "By verifying the lensing object emitted no light, they confirmed it was a black hole weighing about 7.1 times the mass of our Sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gravitational lensing by a black hole.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, STScI, Joseph Olmsted",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gravitational_lensing_by_a_black_hole.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.767,
          "end": 39.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 39.6,
      "end": 49.82,
      "text": "Located about 5,000 light-years away, this phantom is hurtling through space at an estimated speed of 45 to 51 kilometers per second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Flickr via Openverse",
        "title": "An Isolated Black Hole (Illustration)",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://www.flickr.com/photos/144614754@N02/52675793824"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 49.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.82,
      "end": 54.746,
      "text": "An invisible rogue black hole is wandering completely alone through our galaxy.",
